```

### `ParentPortalController` — **mixed** unit-price logic (important inconsistency)

If **`Charge`** and **`SessionCount`** exist, unit price is **`Charge / sessionCount`** (**per session**). If not, it falls back to **`Rate × (durationMinutes / 30)`**, i.e. **`Rate` as price per 30-minute block**, scaled by session length — **not** the same model as `purchaseBatch` / `EnrollmentService` (which treat `Rate` / `price_per_session` as one lump per session).

```540:558:/home/admin/backend/app/Http/Controllers/ParentPortalController.php
    private function resolveUnitPrice(StudentClass $class, int $sessionCount): float
    {
        $charge = (float) ($class->Charge ?? 0);
        if ($charge > 0 && $sessionCount > 0) {
            return $charge / $sessionCount;
        }

        $ratePer30 = (float) ($class->Rate ?? 0);
        if ($ratePer30 > 0) {
            $durationMinutes = max(30, (int) ($class->SessionDuration ?? 120));
            return $ratePer30 * ($durationMinutes / 30);
        }

        $pay = (float) ($class->Pay ?? 0);
        if ($pay > 0 && $sessionCount > 0) {
            return $pay / $sessionCount;
        }

        return 0;
    }
```

